From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] LmbrCentral: skip the lrelease rpath-patch under system Qt6

The bundled Qt deploys its lrelease next to the editor and rewrites the
binary's RPATH from `$ORIGIN/../lib` to `$ORIGIN` (via RPathChange.cmake's
`file(RPATH_CHANGE ...)`) so the copied tool resolves the bundled Qt libs
sitting one directory up.

Under the Fedora system-Qt6 swap (`-DLY_USE_SYSTEM_QT=ON`) the deployed
lrelease is the distribution binary from qt6-qttools. It carries NO
RPATH/RUNPATH and resolves its Qt libraries through the default
`/usr/lib64` loader search, so the rewrite is both unnecessary and fatal:
`file(RPATH_CHANGE ... OLD_RPATH "$ORIGIN/../lib" ...)` requires the old
RPATH to be present in the binary, which the system tool lacks, and the
POST_BUILD step aborts the whole LmbrCentral.Editor link:

  CMake Error at cmake/Platform/Linux/RPathChange.cmake:13 (file):
    file RPATH_CHANGE could not write new RPATH: $ORIGIN to the file
    .../build/bin/profile/lrelease

Caught on the first o3de-experimental system_qt6 build (COPR 10856557,
fedora-44, 2026-08-12), after the engine otherwise compiled and linked
cleanly against system Qt 6.11.1 through 981/3263 steps.

Fix: gate the rpath-patch on `if(NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_QT)`. lrelease is still
deployed via `lrelease_files` below (the TranslationBuilder looks for it
next to the executable at runtime -- TranslationBuilderComponent.cpp), and
with no RPATH it passes Fedora's check-rpaths QA as-is.

Downstream-packaging only; a system-Qt build detail, not an engine bug.
Kept local (gated on the system_qt6 bcond); a system-Qt6 build path does
not exist upstream to pitch this against yet.

Signed-off-by: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
---
--- a/Gems/LmbrCentral/Code/Platform/Linux/lrelease_linux.cmake
+++ b/Gems/LmbrCentral/Code/Platform/Linux/lrelease_linux.cmake
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@
 #
 #

+# Under the Fedora system-Qt6 swap the deployed lrelease is the distro binary
+# (no rpath; finds Qt via /usr/lib64), so the $ORIGIN/../lib rpath-patch is
+# unnecessary and fails. Skip it; lrelease is still deployed via lrelease_files.
+if(NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_QT)
 add_custom_command(TARGET LmbrCentral.Editor POST_BUILD
     COMMAND "${CMAKE_COMMAND}" -P "${LY_ROOT_FOLDER}/cmake/Platform/Linux/RPathChange.cmake"
             "$<TARGET_FILE_DIR:LmbrCentral.Editor>/lrelease"
@@ -14,6 +18,7 @@
     COMMENT "Patching lrelease..."
     VERBATIM
 )
+endif()

 set(lrelease_files
     ${QT_LRELEASE_EXECUTABLE}
